Keep host-specific native shards out of the dependency locks

Armeria pulls in brotli4j, which picks its native binary via an
OS/architecture-activated Maven profile, so a lock written on an arm64 Mac
records native-osx-aarch64 where the CI runner resolves native-linux-x86_64. The
first run of the new check failed on exactly that, in the server and cli locks.

Exclude those native-* shards via dependencyLockModuleFilter so the locks are
host-independent and can be regenerated on any machine -- which matters because
they have to be rewritten after every rebase from upstream. brotli4j itself stays
locked at its real version, so the library is still scanned; only the packaged
binary, which advisories are not issued against, drops out.

Also drop main from the check's triggers -- it only receives merges from develop,
which has already gated the locks.

